Subject: [PATCH] spl: fit: verify image hashes without enabling signatures
Upstream-Status: Pending

Allow the simple FIT loader to check the hash nodes of images it loads
without pulling signature verification and its SPL DM dependencies into
the build. fit_image_verify_with_data() already checks image hashes when
FIT_IMAGE_ENABLE_VERIFY is false; that macro gates only the signature
paths in image-fit.c.

FIT images without hash nodes retain their existing behavior.

---
diff --git a/boot/Kconfig b/boot/Kconfig
--- a/boot/Kconfig
+++ b/boot/Kconfig
@@ -204,3 +204,13 @@
+config SPL_FIT_HASH_VERIFY
+	bool "Verify FIT image hashes in SPL without signature support"
+	depends on SPL_LOAD_FIT
+	help
+	  Verify any hash nodes of each image loaded by the simple FIT loader.
+	  A mismatch or unsupported hash algorithm stops loading the image.
+	  This option does not require FIT signature verification or change
+	  the behavior of images without hash nodes. Enable the hash algorithm
+	  used by the FIT, for example SPL_CRC32 for crc32.
+
 config SPL_FIT_SIGNATURE
 	bool "Enable signature verification of FIT firmware within SPL"
 	depends on SPL_DM
diff --git a/common/spl/spl_fit.c b/common/spl/spl_fit.c
--- a/common/spl/spl_fit.c
+++ b/common/spl/spl_fit.c
@@ -322,7 +322,8 @@ static int load_simple_fit(struct spl_load_info *info, ulong sector,
 		src = (void *)data;	/* cast away const */
 	}
 
-	if (CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(FIT_SIGNATURE)) {
+	if (CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(FIT_SIGNATURE) ||
+	    IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPL_FIT_HASH_VERIFY)) {
 		printf("## Checking hash(es) for Image %s ... ",
 		       fit_get_name(fit, node, NULL));
 		if (!fit_image_verify_with_data(fit, node, gd_fdt_blob(), src,
